.#-----------------------------------------------------
.input|xwiki/2.1
.# Monospace is rendered as code tags, whose content is written as Markdown (and thus escaped, and formatted). A line
.# break directly following the opening tag is written as a line break tag, since the opening tag would start an HTML
.# block otherwise. See monospace2.test for the parsing of the generated Markdown.
.#-----------------------------------------------------
a ##b **c** //d// [[e>>https://www.xwiki.org]] *f* `g` </code> <b>##h

##
i## j

= ##Heading## =

* ##item##
** ##nested
item##

> ##quote##

|=##head##|=b
|##c~|d##|(((
##e##
)))
.#-----------------------------------------------------
.expect|markdown/1.2
.#-----------------------------------------------------
a <code>b **c** _d_ [e](https://www.xwiki.org) \*f\* \`g\` \</code> \<b></code>h

<code><br/>i</code> j

# <code>Heading</code>

* <code>item</code>
    * <code>nested  
item</code>

>  <code>quote</code>

| <code>head</code> |       b        |
| ----------------- | -------------- |
| <code>c\|d</code> | <code>e</code> |
.#-----------------------------------------------------
.expect|event/1.0
